# Build and run

```bash
dotnet build LoanApi.sln -p:SkipNSwag=True
dotnet test LoanApi.sln -p:SkipNSwag=True
dotnet run --project WebApi/WebApi.csproj --launch-profile https
```

- Debug builds of `WebApi` run **NSwag** post-build (OpenAPI + `WebApi/ApiClient/web-api-client.ts`). Use `-p:SkipNSwag=True` for faster/local builds without the NSwag tool.
- Single test: `dotnet test Domain.UnitTests/Domain.UnitTests.csproj --filter "FullyQualifiedName~TypeName.Method"`
- Swagger: `/swagger`. Profiles: http `5041`, https `7233`.
- Dev startup applies migrations + seed → needs SQL Server `localhost\SQLEXPRESS`, or set `"UseInMemoryDatabase": true` in `WebApi/appsettings.json`.
- Seeded admin: `administrator@localhost` / `Administrator1!` (role `Administrator`).

## EF Core

Migrations live in `Infrastructure`; startup project is `WebApi`.

```powershell
$env:SkipNSwag = "True"
dotnet ef migrations add <Name> --project Infrastructure --startup-project WebApi
dotnet ef database update --project Infrastructure --startup-project WebApi
```

`SkipNSwag` must be an **environment variable** for `dotnet ef` (not `-p:`). MSBuild `-p:SkipNSwag=True` does not reach the scaffold host build.
